Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:58:39 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 25/85] render: particle initializers draw the way Wallpaper
 Engine does
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two quiet divergences in the spawn-time initializers, against WE 2.8.485's
spawn interpreter (GH 0x140260d80):

- `colorrandom` drew R, G and B independently, so a red-to-blue range
  also gave greens-free magentas and darks, a noisier, greyer palette.
  WE draws one t and takes min + t·(max − min) for all three channels
  (case 3); the result multiplies the spawn's colour.
- `exponent` was read by sizerandom and angularvelocityrandom only. WE
  reads it in lifetimerandom (case 1), colorrandom (3), alpharandom (6),
  velocityrandom (7, per axis) and rotationrandom (10, per axis) as
  well: the draw is pow(rand, exponent) unless the exponent is exactly 1.
  Lifetimes are at least 0.001 s (case 1).

Origin: ours
Why: off-palette particle colours in 58 of the owner's scenes, lost distribution skew in 25 systems (docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B3: P6, P7)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01288H8YtBieDNWXo3bvfKaP
